    ├── Pitfalls   : pycurl is low-level and verbose; requests/httpx abstract connection pooling, encoding, and error handling; pycurl uses 
    │   libcurl directly; requests uses urllib3; httpx uses httpcore — different underlying behaviors for redirects, retries, timeouts; 
    │   pycurl's WRITEFUNCTION/WRITEDATA pattern maps to response.content in requests/httpx; pycurl's USERPWD maps to auth=(user, pass) in 
    │   requests/httpx; httpx requires explicit `httpx.Client()` for connection reuse; requests uses Session
    └── The code uses pycurl for a single synchronous POST request to retrieve an OAuth access token. Both requests and httpx (in sync mode)
        can replace this with a much simpler API. The usage pattern is basic: set URL, headers, auth, JSON body, read response.

